My older brother Diego sits in the chair.
Our dog is in his arms.
Her name is Lola.
She is a very playful dog.
She sees me on the screen.
She barks loudly.
Diego asks Lola, "Who is this?"
I laugh.
I walk to the window with my phone.
I talk to my dog.
I show the outside view through the window.
Here in Kochi, there are a lot of green trees.
Lola looks at those trees.
She barks again.
Diego asks, "Who is out there?"
I say, "There is no one else here."
I say to my family, "Our home in Mexico is always like this."
"I like this noise of yours very much, and I miss it."
I feel very happy.
